                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A predisposition or natural inclination, propensity, or a predilection; especially, a strong disposition or bent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45fb90b1-6900-4838-b122-04a5be166eba",
                                                "sense_id": "d0033000-f4e5-3fdc-b34f-6a42c38a834c",
                                                "text": "The child has a proclivity for exaggeration."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d58d2c2-46bf-4d6a-9f59-1b65e871d97f",
                                                "sense_id": "d0033000-f4e5-3fdc-b34f-6a42c38a834c",
                                                "text": "This therefore was the reason why the still comparatively young though dissolute man who now addressed Stephen was spoken of by some with facetious proclivities as Lord John Corley."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b496960-f956-426c-a426-ba853f47d7a1",
                                                "sense_id": "d0033000-f4e5-3fdc-b34f-6a42c38a834c",
                                                "text": "The idea is that the choice of x when facing the alternatives #92;#123;x,y#92;#125; reveals a proclivity for choosing x over y that we should expect to see reflected in the individual's behavior when faced with the alternatives #92;#123;x,y,z#92;#125;."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5197601e-ef65-4917-95ac-d96c30fcae56",
                                                "sense_id": "d0033000-f4e5-3fdc-b34f-6a42c38a834c",
                                                "text": "The sermon that morning was ostensibly about healthy sexual relationships, but scathing critiques of capitalism and corporations also got significant airtime. (“I have leftist proclivities,” Brown explained.)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7a76bcd-4586-4460-a03f-8bdbbb750f84",
                                                "sense_id": "d0033000-f4e5-3fdc-b34f-6a42c38a834c",
                                                "text": "A contingent of venture capitalists and entrepreneurs have spurred a rightward shift, leading to the rise of the “Liberaltarian” — a term coined by two Stanford political economists to describe the tech industry’s proclivity toward trumpeting liberalism in some social issues but maintaining antigovernment posturing in regulating businesses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
